  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41123" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">United Nations Industrial Development Organization</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening technical and productive capacities in seven agro industrial chains through good agricultural practices</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In the framework of the Country Programme (CP) Venezuela 2018-2024, UNIDO is providing technical assistance and supporting knowledge transfer on  international best practices and methodological tools in the Bolivarian Republic of Venezuela. UNIDO#s work in the Bolivarian Republic of Venezuela focuses on reactivating the country#s productive apparatus to achieve a more di versified economy by adding value and supporting export promotion of seven selected agro-industrial value chains (corn, rice, legumes, sugar cane, soy, cocoa and coffee). During the implementation of the CP, a comprehensive diagnosis of the seven chains was carried out, action plans were presented and discussed, awareness was raised among stakeholders, and Value Chain Committees were established as spaces for public-private coordination for the efficient implementation of the projects in the framework of the CP. UNIDO presented the results of the diagnoses and action plans to the Development Bank of Latin America (CAF), which has shown interest in contributing to the implementation of priority actions entailed in the action plans. CAF#s contribution shall specifically support UNIDO#s provision of capacity building activities and trainings to actors related to work on primary production and agro-industrial transformation of the prioritized value</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CORPORACION ANDINA DE FOMENTO (CAF)</narrative>
  </participating-org>
